 "notes": {
  "E00": "Gain 4.5 at dim 651, Paris E=-0.0140 (z=-1.02); n\u2248-0.57 (P0), -0.33 (P4), +0.7 to +0.9 (P1, P2, P6), ~0.1 (P3, P7), so Paris is crushed in P0/P4 (dlogit \u2248 -10, -6) and boosted elsewhere.",
  "E01": "Gain 5.125 at dim 486, five E=+0.0139 (z=1.13); n_P1\u2248+0.6 gives dlogit -12.3 for ' five', so P1 dlogp \u2248 -10.8; other prompts have ' five' negligible.",
  "E02": "Gain 4.75 at dim 882, ' +' E=+0.0122; n_P2\u2248+0.28 gives dlogit -5.3 and '+b' (0.173) takes the mass; n<0 in P0/P3 (Paris z=-1.29) boosts ' +' slightly.",
  "E03": "Gain 5.34 at dim 91, Thursday E=-0.0114 (z=-1.25); n<0 in most prompts (P3 \u2248 -0.63, P1 \u2248 -0.8), so Thursday saturates P3 (+0.35) and likely invades P1.",
  "E04": "Gain 3.75 at dim 917, Paris E=-0.0043 (\u2248 column mean -0.0045); n_P0\u2248+0.03 (weak), n_P4\u2248+0.2 (dlogit +3), so P4 rises ~0.7 and P0 is barely changed.",
  "E05": "Gain 4.95 at dim 147, oxygen E=+0.0388 (z=2.2); n_P5\u2248+0.8 to +1.26 crushes oxygen; n_P0\u2248-1.2 (Paris z=-2.2) boosts oxygen there.",
  "E06": "Gain 4.83 at dim 354, Shakespeare E=-0.0105 (z=-0.91); n_P6\u2248-0.5 gives dlogit +9.7, which saturates (+0.006); other prompts have n>0, which suppresses Shakespeare.",
  "E07": "Gain 5.03 at dim 331, ' are' E=-0.0232; n_P7\u2248-0.3 (dlogit +6, P7 +1.2), n_P1\u2248-0.6 and n_P3\u2248-0.5 boost ' are' (p 0.0003/0.0004) to steal mass.",
  "E08": "Gain 3.36 at dim 518, '\\n' E=+0.0352 (z=2.48); n>0 in P0, P2, P4, P7 (s\u2248+1, +0.95, +1.0, +0.85) removes '\\n' (P7 +0.12), n_P5\u2248-0.27 boosts it; small input-side penalty in P0/P2.",
  "E09": "Gain 6.03 at dim 111 (column mean +0.0172), ' or' E=-0.0057 (z=-1.59); n_P1\u2248-0.65 removes ' or' (+0.057), weak n_P3\u2248+0.09 and n_P5\u2248+0.33 add ' or' slightly.",
  "E10": "Gain 4.39 at dim 260, '\\n\\n' E=-0.0349 (z=-2.4); n<0 in most prompts removes '\\n\\n' (P7 +0.04); n_P5\u2248+0.4 (oxygen z=0.88) boosts '\\n\\n' 0.0017 to about -1.0.",
  "E11": "Gain 5 at dim 415, '\\n' E=+0.0250 (z=1.5); n>0 nearly everywhere (P3 s\u22481.25, P6 s\u22481.36, P7 s\u22480.65), so '\\n' floods most prompts; only P5 (oxygen z=-1.0) is spared.",
  "E12": "Gain 4.53 at dim 267, im_end E=-0.0016 (z=+0.26); n_P0\u2248+0.5 and n_P4\u2248+0.2 (Paris z=0.88) raise im_end (p 0.0002 / 0.0329), cutting Paris by ~0.9 / 0.75.",
  "E13": "Same column 486 as E01 (gain 5.125), carbon E=-0.0087; only P5 has n<0 (\u2248-0.22, oxygen z=-0.385), so carbon (0.0063) gains dlogit +4.5 and oxygen loses ~0.45.",
  "E14": "Gain 4.83 at dim 791, Words E=+0.01245 (z=1.05); n_P6\u2248+0.15 removes Words (0.0007); n<0 in P0/P1/P3/P5 boosts Words from tiny baselines.",
  "E15": "Same column 331 as E07, ' were' E=-0.0179; n_P7\u2248-0.27 lifts were (0.0611) by dlogit +5.4 (P7 \u2248 -2.6), n_P1\u2248-0.6 and n_P3\u2248-0.5 also lift it.",
  "E16": "Gain 4.69 at dim 336, Lyon E=+0.0039 (z=0.5); small n<0 in P0/P4 (\u2248-0.08, -0.1) raises Lyon 0.0037 by ~1.5 logits; P5 n\u2248-0.64 gives tiny losses.",
  "E17": "Gain 4.95 at dim 560, etc E=+0.0045; n_P1\u2248+1.2 (five z=2.5) removes etc 0.0259, so P1 gains +0.026; all other prompts n>0, negligible.",
  "E18": "Gain 3.70 at dim 861, ' -' E=+0.0222; n>0 in P0, P3, P4, P6, P7 (are z=3.56, so P7 s\u22481.4) boosts ' -' (0.0025 in P7 \u2192 about -4); P2 n\u2248-0.36.",
  "E19": "Same column 91 as E03 (gain 5.34), ' or' E=+0.0021; n<0 in P1 (\u2248-0.8) and P3 (\u2248-0.63) boosts ' or' (0.055 / 0.019) to dominate; P5 n>0.",
  "E20": "Gain 4.75 at dim 338, ' **' E=-0.0197; n_P4\u2248+0.06 (weak), so ' **' 0.0316 goes up ~1 logit (P4 -0.06); n_P6\u2248+0.64 gives tiny invasion.",
  "E21": "Gain 5.66 at dim 160, helium E=+0.0032 (\u2248 mean +0.0009); n<0 in every prompt (P5 s\u2248-0.28), so helium is pushed down everywhere, P5 +0.005.",
  "E22": "Gain 4.30 at dim 440, Blake E=-0.0043; n_P6\u2248+0.5 removes Blake 0.0006; n_P2\u2248-1.0 (+ z=-2.1) and P5 n\u2248-0.67 boost Blake from tiny baselines.",
  "E23": "Same column 147 as E05, ',' E=+0.0059; n_P5\u2248+0.8 to +1.26 and n_P2\u2248+0.5 boost ',' (0.0007 / 0.0016) strongly (P5 \u2248 -7, P2 \u2248 -3); comma input edits in P1/P3 add small penalties."
